<section id="S3.SS3.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">3.3.2 </span>Ablation Study on Frequency Allocation</h4>

<div id="S3.SS3.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To determine the optimal frequency allocation strategy, we fix the position design the same as MRoPE with <span id="S3.SS3.SSS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">spatial-reset</span> enhancement, and vary only the frequency allocation scheme.
As shown in Table <a href="#S3.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ 3.3.2 Ablation Study on Frequency Allocation ‣ 3.3 Ablation Study ‣ 3 Experiment ‣ Revisiting Multimodal Positional Encoding in Vision–Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, a more uniform allocation strategy consistently outperforms alternatives that split the spectrum into partial chunks.
This highlights the importance of ensuring that each positional axes (time, height, width) retains access to the full frequency spectrum.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S3.T4" class="ltx_table">
