</section>
<section id="A4.SS5.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">D.5.2 </span>Allocation Ratio of Frequency</h4>

<div id="A4.SS5.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS5.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We further investigate different allocation ratios under the interleave frequency strategy. The results are summarized in Table <a href="#A4.T6" title="Table 6 ‣ D.5.2 Allocation Ratio of Frequency ‣ D.5 More Ablation Results. ‣ Appendix D Appendix ‣ Revisiting Multimodal Positional Encoding in Vision–Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>. The balanced allocation (t:h:w = 24:20:20) achieves the best overall performance. Increasing the proportion of channels assigned to the temporal axis reduces the available high-frequency capacity for spatial dimensions. This leads to a degradation in grounding ability and negatively impacts benchmarks involving spatial understanding in both images and videos.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.T6" class="ltx_table">
<table id="A4.T6.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
