<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 7: </span>Comparison of temporal stride settings for video benchmarks on MRoPE-I.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A4.SS5.SSS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS5.SSS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">From the results, <math id="A4.SS5.SSS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta=1</annotation></semantics></math> achieves the best overall performance, while smaller (<math id="A4.SS5.SSS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta=0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta=0.5</annotation></semantics></math>) or larger (<math id="A4.SS5.SSS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta=2</annotation></semantics></math>) strides lead to performance drops. Incorporating the dynamic stride from V2PE does not shows a significant benefit.</p>
</div>
